flowchart TB
    accTitle: How the mutation tests run
    accDescr: Every Saturday, on demand, and for a pull request that changes how they run, the Mutation workflow runs the mutants. For Python, the plan splits the code into parts of about the same number of mutants, and mutmut runs each part in a job of its own, in a copy of the repository and without the tests marked mutation_unsafe; Infection changes the PHP of a Nextcloud app, with the bootstrap of its tests. The summary shows one score and first the survivors that change the logic, with their changes, the artifact keeps them and the dashboard shows the score. When the score of the default branch drops below that of the run before, one issue opens, which closes once a run is back. A run that measured nothing fails and names the tests that failed without any mutant.

    start["Every Saturday · on demand<br>a pull request that changes<br>mutation.yml or mutmut"]
    plan["The plan<br>the Python in parts of<br>about the same number of mutants"]
    python["mutmut, a job for each part<br>in a copy in mutants/<br>without the tests marked mutation_unsafe"]
    php["Infection<br>the PHP of a Nextcloud app<br>with tests/bootstrap.php"]
    score["The summary and the artifact<br>one score · the survivors<br>that change the logic first"]
    dashboard["`The dashboard<br>*mutants caught*`"]
    issue["One issue: Mutation score dropped<br>closes once a run is back"]
    fail["The run fails<br>with the tests that fail<br>without any mutant"]

    start --> plan
    plan --> python
    start --> php
    python -- "mutants ran" --> score
    php -- "mutants ran" --> score
    score --> dashboard
    score -. "the score of main dropped" .-> issue
    python -. "nothing measured" .-> fail
    php -. "nothing measured" .-> fail

    classDef bot fill:#526cfe2e,stroke:#526cfe,stroke-width:2px
    classDef done fill:#16a34a2e,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
    classDef person fill:#f59e0b2e,stroke:#f59e0b,stroke-width:2px
    class plan,python,php bot
    class score,dashboard done
    class issue person
